.TH SDL_GetAudioDeviceProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetAudioDeviceProperties \- Get the properties associated with an audio device.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetAudioDeviceProperties(SDL_AudioDeviceID devid);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This can be used with both logical and physical devices\[char46] Note that while apps can hang any data they want here, physical device IDs are global; it would be better to assign data to one\(aqs own logical device so it doesn\(aqt interfere with other parts of the program that might be using the same physical device ID\[char46]
.PP
Properties provided by SDL for physical devices will also be made available on their associated logical devices, unless otherwise noted\[char46]
.PP
The application can hang any data it wants here, but the following properties are understood by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_AUDIO_DEVICE_UNIQUE_ID_STRING :
This identifier can be used to locate a specific device\[char46] In optimal conditions, this identifier will not change between runs of an app, hardware disconnection, and system reboots\[char46] However, depending on the hardware, operating system, and other circumstances, a device\(aqs identifier may change, so if the app cannot find a device with a previously queried identifier, the user should be prompted to choose a new device (possibly the same device, now with a new identifier)\[char46] Device identifier strings have no specific format, the format may change in the future without warning, and are likely different between different operating systems on the same hardware\[char46] If the system cannot reasonably provide a unique identifier, this property will not be set\[char46] Note that property is useful for finding specific hardware again on a later run of the app, but often times it\(aqs better to just open the default device
.BR "" ( SDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_DEFAULT_PLAYBACK
or
.BR SDL_AUDIO_DEVICE_DEFAULT_RECORDING ),
and let the user set this up globally on their platform\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I devid
the audio device instance id to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

